From 1392b2877f10e03e2469a0e0230273c0159d9af4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:14:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(transactions): fill a transaction from a payment
 screenshot, fully offline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Users can now share a Google Pay / PhonePe / Paytm screenshot into Mercury,
or pick one from the gallery, and have the transaction filled in for them.

Text recognition runs through Google ML Kit on Android and Apple Vision on
iOS. Both ship their models inside the app, so this works with no network
and nothing about a receipt ever leaves the device.

Entry points:
- OS share sheet (image/*), routed to the add-transaction form
- "Scan a payment screenshot" tile on the form, plus a camera option

Nothing is saved automatically. The form is prefilled and the user confirms,
with a banner reporting what was read and flagging partial reads, so an OCR
mistake can never land in the ledger unseen.

Extracted per receipt: amount, expense/income direction, merchant, date, UPI
reference, plus a guessed category (merchant keyword table) and account (bank
hint matched to account names and card tails). Unreadable fields are left
blank rather than guessed.

Parsing is pure and covered by `npm run test:parser` (8 receipt layouts,
including lakh formatting, cashback noise, and identifier-vs-amount cases).

The native modules are loaded defensively: expo-text-extractor throws at
import when unlinked, so it is required lazily. isScanSupported() is false on
web and in Expo Go and the entry tile hides itself, leaving those targets
working as before. Scanning itself needs a development build — see
docs/screenshot-scanning.md, including the patch-package step iOS prebuild
requires.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
