From c81cb224ab240e920734fced7a260343510fe956 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:27:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(scan): stop the add-transaction screen crashing
 without the native module

Opening New transaction threw "Cannot find native module 'ExpoTextExtractor'"
in Expo Go and in any dev build made before the dependency was added.

`expo-text-extractor` calls requireNativeModule at module scope, so merely
importing it throws when the native side is absent. The previous guard tried
to contain that with try/catch around a lazy require, which does not work:
Metro raises the module-init failure through the render path, so it surfaced
as a red-box error regardless of the catch.

Bind the native module with requireOptionalNativeModule instead, which
returns null rather than throwing, and reimplement the one-line file:// URI
wrapper the package applied. Nothing throws now, so there is no error to
escape or to report.

expo-text-extractor stays in package.json: autolinking is what ships the
native code this looks up. Noted in a comment so it is not pruned as unused.

Verified the add-transaction screen renders with the native module absent and
no console errors; the scan tile hides itself as intended.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nvx29DtbUXFULrEKaoKvo2
